+# Schedule P — Register of Policies
+
+Schedule P to P1-001 · a code of the bylaws kept by the Secretary under
+§14.9 and §14.10 · opened by governance registry Entry [n]
+
+> **Draft opening.** This register is proposed together with bylaws
+> §14.8, §14.9, §14.10 and §16.4. It takes effect only when those
+> provisions are adopted and the Secretary opens it by governance registry
+> Entry [n]. Until then no row binds, and every status below is the status
+> proposed for the day of opening. On opening, the Secretary enters rows of
+> classes (a), (d) and (e) and every draft ministerially (§14.10), the
+> published notices (§16.4), and, each as an entry of its own and marked
+> in force, the acts the registry records as valid since 2026-08-31 that
+> made or changed a policy (§16.4). No other row is marked in force,
+> except the rules of this register, which the same act issues.
+
+Every policy of the Institute has one entry here, filed under the bylaws
+section it serves. Only an entry of class (b) or (c) marked in force, or
+a published notice, binds, and only for the version it names. The text of
+the bylaws controls every entry (§14.8). English is authoritative.
+
+## Rules of the register
+
+These rules are the Secretary's procedure for keeping this register
+(§14.9(c), §14.10), issued by the act that opens it, Entry [n]. The
+yearly review in rule 8 is only proposed to the Board; it binds only if
+the Board adopts it as a board policy (§14.10).
+
+1. Where an entry sits: under the section whose subject it puts into
+   practice. A document serving several sections sits once, with pointer
+   rows elsewhere. A document whose subject is unknown sits by its title,
+   or under §14.9.
+2. Columns: Number · Title · Version · Serves · Class · Owner / kept by ·
+   Status · Registry entry · Text (repository @ commit : path).
+3. Status: in force · published notice · vacant · draft · awaiting
+   ratification · superseded · withdrawn · lost · retired · unverified ·
+   informative · cited · pointer.
+4. Numbers: one number, one document, never reissued. Collided numbers
+   keep the bare number for the cited (else most recent) use; other uses
+   take a lowercase suffix in order of first record.
+5. Citing: bylaws sections with the section sign; parts of a policy
+   without it (P2-004 part 3.1). Entries name offices, never people.
+6. Where texts live: NTARI-RAND/Policies, one file per version. Protocol
+   specifications stay beside their code. A Slack canvas, web post,
+   Confluence page or local file is a copy.
+7. Not policies: executive actions (EX-###) and single-matter registry
+   decisions get pointer rows only.
+8. Review: a draft untouched for twelve months is annotated with the date
+   of its last change, and its status stays draft. Proposed to the Board:
+   the Board reviews each board policy yearly, and issuers review their
+   procedures yearly.
+9. Text column: the pinned location where one exists; "to commit and
+   pin" where a text exists, or may yet be found, but is not pinned; "—"
+   where no text exists to pin. A pointer row's text is the row it points
+   to.
+10. Registry entries are cited from the registry of record, the `main`
+    branch of [NTARI-RAND/governance-registry][reg-repo] (Entry 10).
+
+**Classes** (§14.9): (a) cited instruments · (b) board policies ·
+(c) office and federation procedures · (d) informative documents ·
+(e) documents not in force.
+
+**Seats** (§7.2): Covenant = President and Covenant federation.
+Governance = Vice President and Governance federation. Record = Secretary
+and Record federation. Economy & Information = Treasurer and its
+federation. Substrate = Workspace Administrator and Substrate federation.
+
+## How this opening was compiled
+
+The rows follow the placement table of
+[NTARI-RAND/governance-rand#4][gr4], built from an inventory of
+2026-11-13 (61 entries: 52 numbered, 9 unnumbered) and its verification.
+Statuses are carried as that table gives them, except where §16.4
+requires otherwise: the DCO mechanics are marked awaiting ratification,
+and the acts entered at opening say so. Before opening, the Secretary:
+
+- confirms each number suffix, since three documents found only as
+  citations in the bylaws v3.1 draft were added late;
+- re-checks three kinds of fact the inventory reported and nobody
+  re-checked: the 2026-03-18 renumbering proposal, the P2-003 canvas's
+  "[Board resolution required]" line and its Gitee ban, and whether each
+  gen-1 Confluence page is deleted or current;
+- reads the texts the inventory never read, which may hold further
+  policies that need rows: Membership Types, Working Group Charters,
+  Appendices A and B, How Federation Members Vote, NTARI Workflows -
+  Broadcast Specification (canvas F0BB2DXP8CT), an unidentified canvas
+  (F09QYU8PW3S), two proposal canvases, and a "32-policy-governance-voting"
+  file.
+
+Where a row says a rule "moves into the §9.4 text", that happens only if
+§9.4 is amended to carry it; this register does not amend §9.4.
